A||N||4||skitime||Help! 88 V6 Starts hard in the mornings.||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||11-08-2000||08:56 PM||||Help our 88 GT takes extra long to start in the mornings and after it sets for more than a half hour. It starts right up after it already been running a while. It runs fine and idles fine. The plugs were replaced and the cap and rotor replaced as well as the air cleaner. Seems slightly worse now that it is cooler.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-08-2000||09:32 PM||||I'd start by checking the fuel pressure. It is possible that the check valve in the fuel pump has gone bad and the pressure bleeds off when the car sits. Put a guage on the fuel rail and turn the key on to prime the pump, then watch the needle. If it drops down soon after the pump shuts off, you need a new fuel pump or regulator. If you pinch off the return line as soon as the pump shuts off and the pressure still drops, it's the pump. If it holds pressure with the line pinched, it's the regulator. <P>It's also possible that the cold-start injector is not working properly. Not sure how to check that one, except for making sure the wires are connected, and checking the resistance of the injector coil.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||11-08-2000||09:48 PM||||Where is the regulator?  Is it in the fuel pump.  If it is the fuel pump it will have to be replaced I assume.||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||11-08-2000||10:48 PM||||Regulator is not in the fuel pump.  <P>Regulator is the diaphragm-looking thing on top of the fuel rail, where the fuel supply and return lines are.  It has a single vacuum line going to it, also.<P>If fuel pump is bad, I believe it must be replaced.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||11-09-2000||12:46 AM||||cold start injector is probably dirty or no good, check it!<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
